    {
      "argv": [
        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm-0dd4b1255/dist/cli.js",
        "In src/index.ts the LRUCache constructor's TTL initialization defines a local helper, setPurgetTimer, that clears and reschedules the per-entry autopurge timeout; it is called from the setItemTTL and updateItemAge closures. Today the helper always runs its clearTimeout/setTimeout logic, even when the cache was created without ttlAutopurge, in which case purgeTimers is undefined and every call does nothing useful. Restructure the helper so that the decision is made once at construction time: bind setPurgetTimer to a no-op function when this.ttlAutopurge is falsy, and to the existing timer-managing arrow function otherwise, using a single conditional expression written exactly as `!this.ttlAutopurge ?` followed by the no-op branch and then the real implementation. Structural requirement: after the change the regex `!this\\.ttlAutopurge \\?` must match exactly once in src/index.ts (it matches zero times today), and the identifier setPurgetTimer must still appear exactly three times (its definition and its two call sites). Behavior must be unchanged: the full tap suite must pass as it does today, TTL autopurge must still expire entries when ttlAutopurge is true, and no public API, exported type or test or snapshot file may be modified.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run prepare && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npx tap\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
